/*
  core/masks/confirm_behavior.spthy -- f_H for the CONFIRM action class (approval prompts), AGNOSTIC_MASKS.md.
  Collapses attentive_approve / busy_approve / careless_approve / habituated_approve. The ceremony
  reports only OBSERVABLES in !StepData(P,pid,<claimed, own>) -- the intent the prompt claims to
  authorize vs the user's OWN pending intent (the login/request they actually initiated; an
  unforgeable fresh token when they initiated nothing). The VERDICT is derived HERE, in the response
  layer: the Attentive rule PERFORMS the self-check (matches claimed = own), it does not read a
  producer-declared 'self'/'injected' oracle tag -- same observables discipline as the compare class
  (repo MEMORY.md lesson 14). Injected(pid) stays the PRODUCER's provenance action, lemma vocabulary
  only; the lemmas read the action facts Approve/AutoApprove as before.

    Attentive  ('verify-self') : fires only when claimed = own (the pattern <k,k>) -> on an injected
      prompt NO rule fires (the user has no matching intent and rejects).
    Busy/Habituated ('autoapprove') : reflexively approve ANY prompt without looking -> AutoApprove
      (a Shutout / ShutoutBlocksAutoApprove mitigation gates this on a Shutout-protected prompt).
    Careless ('dismiss') : times out, no approval.

  The two APPROVE outcomes emit a generic Confirmed(P,pid,mask) so a ceremony where the approval GATES a
  downstream action (e.g. a device signature) can consume it via a thin effect adapter --
  the same output+adapter pattern as compute (Respond) and compare (Checked). Where unused it dangles
  harmlessly. RespMask(P,mask) gated by mask_state.spthy as before; Approve(P,pid,mask) carries the mask.
*/

// Attentive: performs the self-check -- fires only when the claimed intent equals the user's own.
rule Confirm_attentive_verify [color=#27ae60]:
    [ !Step(P, pid, 'confirm'), !StepData(P, pid, <k, k>), !OutcomePolicy(mask, 'confirm', 'verify-self') ]
  --[ Approve(P, pid, mask), RespMask(P, mask), Verified(P, pid), Answered(pid) ]->
    [ Confirmed(P, pid, mask) ]

// Busy / Habituated: reflexively approve ANY prompt (incl. an injected one -> prompt-bombing).
rule Confirm_autoapprove [color=#27ae60]:
    [ !Step(P, pid, 'confirm'), !OutcomePolicy(mask, 'confirm', 'autoapprove') ]
  --[ Approve(P, pid, mask), RespMask(P, mask), AutoApprove(P, pid), Mask(P,'Attentive',mask), Answered(pid) ]->
    [ Confirmed(P, pid, mask) ]

// Careless: dismisses the prompt without acting -> timeout, no approval (safe-fail).
rule Confirm_dismiss [color=#27ae60]:
    [ !Step(P, pid, 'confirm'), !OutcomePolicy(mask, 'confirm', 'dismiss') ]
  --[ Approve(P, pid, mask), RespMask(P, mask), Timeout(P), Answered(pid) ]->
    [ ]
